<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dutch</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dutch are the people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, who became a leading maritime and commercial power in the seventeenth century. Through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> and its trading companies they competed with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>, traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a>, and dealt with African states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>His capital, Bandar Aceh Darussalam near the mouth of the Aceh River, later called Kutaraja by the <b>Dutch</b> and now Banda Aceh, became the seat of a dynasty that identified itself firmly with Islam.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aceh-sultanate">Aceh Sultanate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The founding context was one of subjugation: the Asante states of the interior paid tribute to Denkyira, a powerful forest kingdom to the south-west that controlled their access to the coast and to European trade goods, particularly firearms obtained through the <b>Dutch</b> at Elmina.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The reports of French and <b>Dutch</b> visitors made Siam one of the best-described Asian kingdoms in early modern Europe.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya Kingdom · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Chronic inflation was tamed in the early 2000s and a new manat launched on 1 January 2006, but demand pushed inflation to 16.6 percent in the first quarter of 2007, and the economy shows signs of '<b>Dutch</b> disease'.</blockquote><a href="/empire/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Commercially, Benin's position between the forest interior and the Atlantic coast made it an important partner in Portuguese, <b>Dutch</b> and British commercial networks from the fifteenth to the nineteenth centuries, and its demand for brass manillas stimulated European metal production on a large scale.</blockquote><a href="/empire/benin-empire">Benin Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The Peace of Amiens returned the Cape to the Batavian Republic in 1803, but a British force under General David Baird landed again and won the Battle of Blaauwberg on 8 January 1806, and the Netherlands formally ceded the colony in the Anglo-<b>Dutch</b> convention of 1814.</blockquote><a href="/empire/cape-colony">Cape Colony · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
